                <pb facs="0162" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C114/835a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-30T18:00:00-04:00">August 30, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>97. Department’s telegram No. 84, August 14, 11 a.m. Can you ascertain,
                    discreetly, whether Sir Eric will show the message contained <pb facs="0163"
                        n="27" xml:id="pg27"/> in Department’s telegram under reference to Council
                    of the League, and if he will, at what moment? Is it your opinion that when
                    Council discusses this message, there will be likelihood that its contents will
                    become known to press at Geneva? Please give Department advance notice of this,
                    if possible. It would be better for the situation here, obviously, if no
                    publicity were given, as premature discussion of the matter over here might well
                    be harmful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
